---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Mission — Mad River AI"
  description="What Mad River AI is, why we exist, and the principles that drive the work."
  ogTitle="Mission & Goals"
  ogSubtitle="Automate the research work a careful human would do."
  ogEyebrow="mission"
>
  <article class="px-6 md:px-12 py-20 max-w-3xl">
    <p class="font-mono text-sm tracking-widest text-amber-soft uppercase mb-6">
      Mission & Goals
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-6xl font-semibold leading-tight mb-12">
      <span class="gradient-text">Automate the research work</span><br />
      <span class="text-ink-50">a careful human would do.</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="text-xl text-ink-200 leading-relaxed mb-8">
      Mad River AI exists because knowledge work has exploded in volume
      but not in tooling. Researchers, analysts, investigators, and
      curious humans still do most of the synthesis, cross-referencing,
      and provenance tracking by hand — slowly, with notes that don't
      talk to each other, and with no audit trail.
    </p>
    <p class="text-xl text-ink-200 leading-relaxed mb-12">
      We build agents that do this work — but
      <em>faster, repeatable, and with provenance baked in</em>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl mt-16 mb-6">Our principles</h2>
    <ol class="space-y-6">
      <li class="flex gap-4">
        <span class="text-amber-glow font-mono text-sm mt-1">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg mb-1">Local-first</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-200 leading-relaxed">
            No data leaves your machine unless you tell it to. No
            telemetry. No "phone home." You own the provenance log.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-4">
        <span class="text-amber-glow font-mono text-sm mt-1">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg mb-1">Human-in-the-loop</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-200 leading-relaxed">
            Every agent can be paused, inspected, and overridden. No
            black boxes. Every claim links back to its source.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-4">
        <span class="text-amber-glow font-mono text-sm mt-1">03</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg mb-1">Provenance</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-200 leading-relaxed">
            Every piece of data is tagged with where it came from and
            when. Replayable. Auditable. Defensible.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-4">
        <span class="text-amber-glow font-mono text-sm mt-1">04</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg mb-1">Composable</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-200 leading-relaxed">
            Tasks are small. Pipelines are explicit. Agents are just
            pipelines with memory. You can re-mix the parts.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-4">
        <span class="text-amber-glow font-mono text-sm mt-1">05</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg mb-1">Legal by design</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-200 leading-relaxed">
            Every tool ships with a legal note. The runtime refuses to
            load a tool whose note is missing. No doxxing, no stalking,
            no harassment — by design.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl mt-16 mb-6">Where we're going</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-ink-200">
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="text-amber-glow">→</span>
        <span><strong>v0.2 of the framework.</strong> Real-LLM synthesis, YAML pipeline runner, full provenance chain via parent_id linking.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="text-amber-glow">→</span>
        <span><strong>Hosted agent surface.</strong> A web UI on top of the runtime. "Type a question, get a sourced synthesis." API first, then UI.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="text-amber-glow">→</span>
        <span><strong>More lanes.</strong> Academic literature (live), company investigation, market intelligence, due diligence.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="text-amber-glow">→</span>
        <span><strong>Open-source core forever.</strong> The framework stays MIT. The interesting bits — paid data sources, customer UX — live in private repos and ship as managed services.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>
